{
  "rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underprediction: when the last ~5–10 days show a sustained rise, the model systematically forecasts too low and too flat. Apply an upward level shift that grows with horizon (small at days 1–3, large by days 10–30).",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: errors increase with lead time; near-term (1–3d) is close, but medium/long horizons (7–30d) are materially below realized prices. Use a ramping correction (additive spread widening with forecast step).",
    "Lag in regime shifts: after a breakout from the mid/high-60s into the 70s+, the model behaves as if prices will revert back to the prior range. Add a 'regime-change' rule: if price breaks above recent 20–30d range, reduce mean-reversion strength and lift the whole path.",
    "Over-mean-reversion after spikes: following sharp up moves, the model pulls forecasts back toward ~68–71, but outcomes continue trending higher. Replace mean reversion with trend-following when momentum is positive (e.g., positive slope over last 5–10 days).",
    "Volatility/convexity underestimation: realized paths show larger upside extension than forecast (tops in high-70s/80s vs forecasts stuck ~70). Inflate upside tail/volatility in bullish regimes (e.g., widen bands or add convex uplift to later horizons)."
  ]
}
